[
  "ACT 1: COLD OPEN & PERSONAL GROUNDING [00:00 - 03:00]\nScene: 01. Starting Soon -> 02. Monologue / Full Camera\n\nWelcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The Practice and the Dojo. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers in Chicago were building grassroots rooms to escape corporate silos. Today we rewatch Episode 11: Justin Searls from SCNA 2012 (2012).",
  "ACT 2: SETTING THE HISTORICAL SCENE [03:00 - 08:00]\nScene: 02. Monologue / Full Camera\n\nJustin Searls was a major recurring voice at SCNA Chicago, using sharp humor and deep empathy to help developers laugh at their own architectural excesses. When we recorded this in 2012, there were no corporate sponsor filters. Developers were meeting after hours, sharing hard-won lessons on deliberate practice and system boundaries.",
  "ACT 3: THE CORE INQUIRY: THE SOUND ABOVE [08:00 - 14:00]\nScene: 02. Monologue / Full Camera -> 04. Split Screen\n\nWhat inspired Justin Searls to challenge dogma in test-driven development? How did Test Double pioneer a humane, empathetic model of consulting that prioritized team health over rigid doctrine? Who inspired Justin Searls before they stepped onto this stage? What records were playing in the background when this movement formed?",
  "ACT 4: HALLWAY REWATCH & VIDEO REACTION [14:00 - 28:00]\nScene: 03. Reaction - Video Focus\n\nRoll archive footage (YouTube ID: 6JB7o8I4Uy4). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "ACT 5: THE AI-ERA PARALLEL & TERMINAL WORKBENCH [28:00 - 40:00]\nScene: 05. Workbench - Code & Terminal\n\nDogma is the enemy of effectiveness. As AI enters the software lifecycle, blindly applying 2010 testing rituals without understanding their purpose creates brittle friction. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "ACT 6: COMMUNITY CODA, OUTRO & NEXT STREAM [40:00 - 45:00]\nScene: 08. Outro & Next Stream\n\nThank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 12. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]